{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790291631,"nonce":"HY6o5ZD3gkYk+WmMKDjVl5uLU48=","title":"wasm: await on a host bridge never completes; browser suite never ran in Chrome","message":"tests/browser_smoke.rs has no wasm_bindgen_test_configure!, so wasm-bindgen-test-runner defaults to Node and `wasm-pack test --headless --chrome` prints \"only configured to run in node.js ... skipping\". CI's Chrome step has run zero tests, including in the last green run (32572314441, 2026-08-22). The runner selects the browser when WASM_BINDGEN_USE_BROWSER is set; CI now sets it.\n\nRun for real (Chrome 153 or `wasm-pack test --node`), 11 of 13 pass and both awaits time out (\"5s timeout, complete_task never fired\"): run_async_with_sleep_yields_and_returns_42 and run_async_arithmetic_then_await_returns_42.\n\nCause: `main$poll` fails on its first poll with `type mismatch: expected integer (AsyncSaveSlot value), got Undef`. HIR before krio:\n\n    %v2 = call sym \"__zyntax_async_set_timeout\"(%v0)\n    call intrinsic.decref(%v2)\n    call intrinsic.incref(%v2)\n    %v3 = call intrinsic.await(%v2)\n    ...\n    call intrinsic.drop(%v2)\n\nThe ARC memory pass (default CompilationConfig) puts ownership ops on every pointer-typed value. The krio host-bridge rewrite (lower_host_bridge_await_site) drops the bridge call's result binding, but the decref/incref stay, and liveness saves %v2 across the suspension because of the trailing drop. So the poll fn saves an undefined value.\n\nThe error never surfaced: zyntax_wasm's call_indirect_by_handle maps Err to 0, which reads as Pending (separate issue).\n\nFix: krio_adapter::abi_emit::strip_host_bridge_ownership_ops removes IncRef/DecRef/Drop on an awaited `__zyntax_async_*` result. apply_krio_async_lowering runs it on each async fn before liveness. Regression test: krio_adapter stages_i2_host_bridge_await::host_bridge_await_value_keeps_no_ownership_ops.","files":null}]}